Trademarks
----------

"VTK", "Visualization Toolkit" and "Kitware" identify a project and a company
this archive is not part of. They are used only to describe what is archived.


Personal data, and raising a concern
-----------------------------------

Author names and usernames are reproduced as they appear on the original
pages, because an unattributed archive of a discussion is a worse record than
no archive. Profile email addresses returned by GitLab's API are discarded
before anything is stored.

Anyone with a concern about something published here can open an issue:
https://github.com/pyvista/vtk-archive/issues/new?template=removal-request.yml

Personal data, and material that should not have been public in the first
place, is removed on request from the person it concerns. Everything else is a
public technical discussion that this archive exists to preserve, so a request
to remove it is read on its merits rather than granted automatically. Nothing
removed here is removed from gitlab.kitware.com, which remains the original
and authoritative copy.


Collection
----------

Collected through GitLab's public REST API using an ordinary user account with
read-only (read_api) access to a public project. Requests are sequential, with
a delay, never concurrent. The collector identifies itself honestly as
"vtk-archive/0.1 (+https://github.com/pyvista/vtk-archive; archival mirror)".
No bot protection was circumvented; where an endpoint admits only certain
clients, this archive goes without the data rather than claiming to be one.

A purpose of this archive is to absorb automated traffic that would otherwise
fall on gitlab.kitware.com, which Kitware funds and maintains for VTK's
development.
